Package: charr
Title: Simple, Consistent Wrappers for Common String Operations, with
    ALTREP Interoperability
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Travers", "Ching", , "traversc@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Hadley", "Wickham", , "hadley@posit.co", role = c("aut", "cph"),
           comment = "Author of stringr, of which charr is a fork"),
    person("Posit Software, PBC", role = c("cph", "fnd"),
           comment = "Copyright holder of stringr")
  )
Description: An experimental hard fork of the 'stringr' package with an
    ALTREP-aware native string engine built on 'charport'. With the
    backend switch off (the default), every operation delegates to
    'stringi' and behavior is identical to 'stringr'. With it on,
    eligible operations read ALTREP character vectors through the
    'charport' interface without materializing them, and fall back to
    'stringi' wherever the native engine cannot guarantee identical
    results.
